                <pb facs="0907" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg779"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 589.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Valera</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 8,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 28th ultimo,
                    as to a possible expedition to be set on foot in this country, against the peace
                    of the island of Cuba, I have the honor to say that the attorney of the United
                    States at New York has been directed to exercise all possible vigilance to
                    discover and use means to prevent any violation of the neutrality laws in the
                    direction indicated.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
